# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Alert Routing Agent — optional configuration
#
# YOU DO NOT NEED TO FILL THIS IN.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# is enough. Every command in the README, all four demo scenarios, the HTTP
# surface and the entire test suite run with both values blank. There is no
# "mock mode" flag to set, because there is no live-mode to fall back FROM: the
# transports are simulated by design (see "What is unfinished" in the README),
# so nothing in this project can send a real Slack message, email or SMS.
#
# This file therefore lists exactly two variables — the only two the code reads.
# There is no SLACK_BOT_TOKEN or TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN here because there is no
# Slack or Twilio integration to hold one, and a template advertising
# credentials the code never reads would be a lie that costs a reviewer ten
# minutes.
#
# Verify that claim yourself:  grep -rn "os.getenv" alert_router/
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Optional. Blank is a supported, tested configuration.
#
# With it blank, notification bodies are produced by render_template() — the
# deterministic renderer, which is what the tests assert against and what the
# audit trail labels `via template`.
#
# With a key set, the same text is handed to the model to rephrase. The model is
# TOLD the decision: it gets no candidate list, no scores and no authority to
# change the recipient, channel or role. If the call fails for any reason the
# system falls back to the template and names the failure in the audit trail
# rather than degrading silently.
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Optional. Only consulted when OPENAI_API_KEY is set.
OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-5.5
